WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.560
Unsupported software matters because applications often enforce identity, access,

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:09.460
data handling, business workflows, and service integrations.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:15.440
Teams should evaluate this issue across user-facing features, APIs, administrative tools,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.540
cloud services, and delivery pipelines.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:23.640
Dependency risks matters because applications often enforce identity, access,

00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:27.380
data handling, business workflows, and service integrations.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:31.920
Vulnerable third-party libraries matters because applications often enforce identity,

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:36.620
access, data handling, business workflows, and service integrations.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:42.440
Supply chain concerns matters because applications often enforce identity, access,

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.260
data handling, business workflows, and service integrations.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.200
Patch management Dependency scanning Software inventory management Selected CIS Controls

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:56.540
mappings for this topic include Control 7 - Continuous Vulnerability Management;

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:03.880
7.1 - Establish vulnerability management process; 7.2 - Remediate vulnerabilities;

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:07.620
7.4 - Application vulnerability scanning.
